const e="kerala-university-youth-festival",m=2025,a="Read in full: the Kerala University Youth Festival Rules 2024 (21 PDF pages; Schedule II item lists are printed partly in images and in Malayalam, read from rendered pages and translated, original term in brackets the first time), the identical 2025 rules file, and the 2025 festival brochure (8 image pages: dates, venues, programme by day, committees). The rules print no entry fee, no phone number, no e-mail, no address, no age or class limit, no fixed dates for the festival, no bank account, and no judging aspects for Debate, Elocution, Essay Writing, Short Story Writing, Poetry Writing, Quiz, Cartooning, Rangoli, Collage and Poster Making (their rows say so). The 2025 rules file and the website list 2025 dates (28 to 31 May 2025 in Kollam); the rules say the University festival is held before the Christmas holidays. The newer value is in the Variables EventStartDate and EventEndDate, the rule is kept as UniversityFestivalTiming. The template cites Rule 2(b) for 'any bonafide full-time student enrolled for a degree, postgraduate degree or diploma course'; the rules text defines only a College under Rule 2(b) and prints no such wording, so no such sentence is captured. Margamkali: Schedule I and the judging text print 7 members, the certificate amendment names 6 performers and 1 accompanist; both are kept. Thiruvathira: Schedule I prints 10 members; certificates go to at most 8 performers and 2 accompanists. The Brochure lists a Drama programme on 30 May 2025 that is not an item of Schedule I; it is only in the news Variable. The brochure's contact persons are public office bearers; no phone number is printed. The brochure says 116 cultural events; the template holds 61 titles because each language and gender version of an item is one title (Schedule I numbers 102 items).",t=JSON.parse(`{"Title":"Rules & Criteria","Subtitle":"Kerala University Youth Festival. Read these rules before you register.","NoticeTitle":"Please Read Before Registering","Notice":"The Kerala University Youth Festival is held at the college level and the University level. Colleges register through the Kerala University Union.","Notes":["The entry form signed by the Principal and the Arts Club Secretary must reach the Kerala University Union by {{EntryFormDeadline}}.","Only participants with a valid identity from the Department of Student Services can take part.","Give any complaint in writing to the Convener of the appellate Committee within an hour of the result. Complaints about the marks are not accepted.","Make-up and accompaniments are arranged by the teams. The festival committee gives the stage and the stage equipment."],"Sections":[{"Key":"general","Title":"General Rules","Items":["These rules are called the Kerala University Youth Festival Rules.","The rules codify and co-ordinate the rules for the competitions held in the Youth Festivals at the college level and at the University level.","The rules apply to the Youth Festivals held at the college level and at the University level.","Competitions are held in the items listed in Schedule I, at the college level and at the University level.","In these rules a College means any educational institution that is maintained by or affiliated to the University of Kerala. A Judge is a person appointed to pronounce a decision in a contest or competition.","The Syndicate of the University can make any amendments to the rules.","The steering committee can make any change in the date of the University Youth Festival.","The University Departments at Thiruvananthapuram and Kariavattom are treated as a single unit for taking part in the University Youth Festival.","Stage and stage equipment are provided by the festival committee. Make-up, accompaniments and the like are arranged by the participating teams themselves.","The sale of video or CD of the events is banned at the venue of the festival.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given to every item, including music.","In music items a Sruthi Box can be used. A pick up can be used for Veena, Guitar, Violin and other instruments where the item rows say so.","Items were added over the years by Syndicate decisions: in 1999 and 2010; in 2013 (Kerala Nadanam male, female and group; Tabala; Veena; Ganamela; Vrindavadyam; Margamkali; Hindi Elocution; English and Hindi Recitation; Guitar; Kathakali and Ottamthullal separately; Mimicry; Mono Act; Hindustani Classical Vocal; Gazal; Folk Song; Mappilappattu; Chenda; Essay Writing and Poetry Writing in English and Hindi; Spot Photography; Poster Making); in 2017 (Vanchipattu, Chakyarkoothu, Nangyarkoothu); in 2018 (Tamil Elocution, Essay Writing, Poetry Writing and Short Story Writing); and in 2020 (Vattapattu, Arabanamuttu).","The word Achumbithasayam in the judging aspects is replaced with the word Mauliksayam (originality of idea).","Kathaprasangam is moved from the Literary Events to the Theatre Events. It has separate competitions for male and female.","Kuchipudi is a separate item for male and female. It replaces other forms of classical dance in the Dance section.","Skit allows a minimum of 2 participants and a maximum of 6 participants.","Dance items: a live orchestra is used in Kathakali and Ottamthullal. For the other dance forms recorded music must be used."]},{"Key":"eligibility","Title":"Eligibility","Items":["The rules apply to Youth Festivals at the college level and the University level, for the colleges that are maintained by or affiliated to the University of Kerala. A college sends its participants to the University Youth Festival.","Only participants who are identified by the Department of Student Services can take part in the University Youth Festival. The stage manager checks that the candidate has a valid identity issued by the Department of Student Services.","Normally a college selects one student for each item to represent the college in the University Youth Festival.","The college level committee can send one more student in a particular item if it is satisfied with the competence of the second candidate. This discretion is used very judiciously and is applied for not more than five items (the earlier limit was two items).","A participant can compete in at most seven individual items (the earlier limit was five).","No competition need normally be held in an item at the college level if there are fewer than 2 competitors in the item. If the college level committee is satisfied that the standard of the performances is high, the student can still be presented for the University Youth Festival.","The minimum number of participants for any event is three, except for the events in which transgender students take part.","Transgender students studying under the University can take part in the University Youth Festival. They can register in any item as an additional category and are evaluated separately.","Team strength is set for each group item in Schedule I. Thiruvathira, Oppana, Margamkali are for girls only, and Dufmutt, Kolkali, Vattapattu and Arabanamuttu are for boys only (see the item rows).","A college can send two staff members and the Secretary of the Arts Club along with its contingent, in addition to the participants."]},{"Key":"registration","Title":"How to Register","Items":["Colleges register their participants for the University Youth Festival by sending the entry form signed by the Principal and the Secretary of the Arts Club.","The entry form must reach the General Secretary, Kerala University Union, not later than {{EntryFormDeadline}}.","College level competitions are held {{CollegeLevelTiming}}.","The college level competitions are held under a committee of the Principal, the Staff Advisor, the College Union Chairman, the General Secretary of the College Union and the Secretary of the Arts Club. The Principal or the nominee and 2 other members make the quorum.","The University level Youth Festival is held {{UniversityFestivalTiming}}. The venue is fixed by the Kerala University Union.","Every participant must hold a valid identity issued by the Department of Student Services. The stage manager checks it.","Each college is represented by one student for each item, with a second student in some items as the Eligibility section says."]},{"Key":"levels","Title":"Levels and Judges","Items":["The Youth Festival has two levels: the college level and the University level.","College level: the Principal appoints the judges from a panel prepared by the college committee. The judges are persons of proven proficiency in the field.","College level: no person is appointed as a judge if he or she is related to any of the competitors or is interested in any other manner.","College level: the committee that runs the college level competitions is also the appellate body. Any complaint about the selection of the candidate for the University Youth Festival goes to this committee, and its decision is final.","University level: a steering-cum-appellate Committee set up by the Syndicate supervises and controls the festival. Members: the Pro-Vice Chancellor (Chairman); three members of the Syndicate nominated by the Vice-Chancellor, one of whom is the student member of the Syndicate; the Chairman and the General Secretary of the Kerala University Union; the Dean of Fine Arts; the Director of Student Services (Convener).","The Chairman and 3 other members make the quorum. If the Pro-Vice-Chancellor is absent, the student member of the Syndicate is the Chairman.","University level: the steering Committee prepares separate panels of judges for different items, and the University Union invites judges only from those panels. Judges are persons of proven proficiency in the field. No person is a judge if related to any competitor or interested in any other manner.","If judges from the panel are not available, the Union can invite judges from outside the panel with the prior sanction of the Pro-Vice-Chancellor.","No judge can judge the competitions of the Kerala University Youth Festival for more than two consecutive years. The identity and the field of expertise of the judges are announced at the start of each event by the stage managers."]},{"Key":"points","Title":"Points and Championship","Items":["For all items except group items, the points are 5 for the first place, 3 for the second place and 1 for the third place.","For group items, the points are 10 for the first place, 6 for the second place and 2 for the third place.","Points scored in group items are not counted to decide the individual championships.","There is one individual champion among boys and one among girls, decided on the total points scored by the individuals. In case of a tie, the actual percentage of marks scored by the competitors decides.","There is an individual champion titled Kalarathnam among the transgender students who score the highest points in their category. If there is a tie even after applying the same norm, the championship is decided by lot.","The team championship is decided on the total points scored by the college.","A Special appreciation award is given to the Women's College that secures the maximum points in the Kerala University Youth Festival."]},{"Key":"prizes","Title":"Prizes and Awards","Items":["First, second and third prizes are given in each item (see Judges and Judging for how they are decided).","Individual champion among boys, individual champion among girls, the Kalarathnam title for the transgender students, and the team championship of colleges are given as the Points section says.","The Special appreciation award is given to the Women's College that secures the maximum points.","The 2025 programme had a prize distribution on the last day (see the news item)."]},{"Key":"payments","Title":"Expenses","Items":["The actual travelling and food expenses of the contingent of a college are met from the college union fund."]},{"Key":"conduct","Title":"Conduct","Items":["No acting, speech or other expression that makes the audience feel disgust or dislike is allowed in any item.","The national anthem must not be insulted.","Obscene or vulgar speech or expression must not be said or shown.","No expression that damages the unity and integrity of the nation is allowed.","No performance that hurts religious feelings is allowed.","The performance must show a high cultural standard.","The steering-cum-appellate Committee can disqualify any participant or team for gross misbehaviour or for violation of the rules.","If a team or an individual backs out at the time of staging, they must prove the reason before the Appellate Committee. If the reason is not genuine, the Appellate Committee disqualifies the participants and the result is declared as per the judgment."]},{"Key":"judging","Title":"Judging and Results","Items":["The prizes for different items are given on the average of the marks of the 3 judges. The marks given by different judges should generally not differ by more than 20 percent.","If the difference between the highest mark and the lowest mark of the three judges is more than 20 percent, the highest or the lowest mark (as the case may be) is not counted. The average of the two marks whose difference is not more than 20 percent is taken.","If the differences between the marks of all three judges are more than 20 percent, the two marks with the smallest difference are taken as the basis and their average is taken.","There must be no overwriting in the scoring sheets of the judges. A correction must be fully signed by the judge.","After an event the judges give the scoring sheets to the stage managers appointed by the steering-cum-appellate Committee, who tabulate the marks and announce the result.","The tabulation and announcement of the results are made in the presence of all three judges, or at least one judge of the event. All the judges countersign the tabulation sheet of the event.","The scoring sheets, tabulation sheets and other papers of an item are put in sealed covers as soon as the result of the item is announced. They are kept in the safe custody of the Director of Student Services."]},{"Key":"complaints","Title":"Complaints and Appeals","Items":["The steering-cum-appellate Committee can consider any complaint received in writing from a candidate about the conduct of the Youth Festival. It can call for any record that it finds relevant.","A complaint in writing must be given to the Convener of the appellate Committee within an hour of the announcement of the result.","The appellate Committee takes the final decision on the matter.","A complaint about the marks given by the judges is not entertained by the appellate Committee.","The sealed covers of the scoring sheets are opened only in the presence of the appellate Committee."]},{"Key":"other","Title":"Other Points","Items":["The rules print no entry fee, no phone number, no e-mail address and no venue address. The University lists the results, the rules and the programme on the festival website {{EventWebsite}}.","The rules also hold the history of when each item was added (Syndicate decisions of 1984, 1989, 1999, 2010, 2013, 2015, 2017, 2018, 2019, 2020 and 2023). They are not repeated here."]}],"Documents":[{"Title":"Kerala University Youth Festival Rules 2024 (PDF)","Url":"https://kuyf.keralauniversity.ac.in/images/Youth-Festival-Rules-2024.pdf"},{"Title":"Youth Festival Rules 2025 (PDF)","Url":"https://kuyf.keralauniversity.ac.in/images/Youth-Festival-Rules-2025.pdf"},{"Title":"Youth Festival 2025 brochure and official schedule (PDF)","Url":"https://kuyf.keralauniversity.ac.in/images/Youth_festival_2025_official_schedule.pdf"},{"Title":"Kerala University Youth Festival website","Url":"https://kuyf.keralauniversity.ac.in/"}]}`),n=[{ParticipantType:"Individual",Source:"Rules 23 and 25, p.4",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:null,Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:["First place 5 points, second place 3 points, third place 1 point.","The points of the individual items decide the individual championships."],Notes:null},Markdown:`## Points
- First place 5 points, second place 3 points, third place 1 point.
- The points of the individual items decide the individual championships.`},{ParticipantType:"Team",Source:"Rules 24 and 25, p.4",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:null,Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:["First place 10 points, second place 6 points, third place 2 points.","Points scored in group items are not counted for the individual championships. They count for the team championship of the college."],Notes:null},Markdown:`## Points
- First place 10 points, second place 6 points, third place 2 points.
- Points scored in group items are not counted for the individual championships. They count for the team championship of the college.`}],i=[{AgeGroup:"Students",Source:"Rules 2(b), 7 and Amendments 7",Sections:{About:["The participants take part through colleges maintained by or affiliated to the University of Kerala, and are identified by the Department of Student Services."],TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:null,Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:["The rules print no age limit and no class limit. The template shows one group for all the students."]},Markdown:`## About this competition
- The participants take part through colleges maintained by or affiliated to the University of Kerala, and are identified by the Department of Student Services.

## Notes for participants
- The rules print no age limit and no class limit. The template shows one group for all the students.`}],o=JSON.parse('[{"Title":"Light Music","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 1-2 and Rules, Schedule II 1 & 2","Sections":{"About":["Solo. Separate competitions are held for male and female participants."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 5 minutes."],"Rules":["A Sruthi Box can be used.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider expression (bhavam), rhythm (layam) and pronunciation (uccharanam)."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo. Separate competitions are held for male and female participants.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A Sruthi Box can be used.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider expression (bhavam), rhythm (layam) and pronunciation (uccharanam)."},{"Title":"Classical Music","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 3-4 and Rules, Schedule II 3 & 4","Sections":{"About":["Solo. Separate competitions are held for male and female participants."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 10 minutes."],"Rules":["A Sruthi Box can be used.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider rhythm (talam), improvisation (manodharmam) and expression (bhavam)."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo. Separate competitions are held for male and female participants.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A Sruthi Box can be used.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider rhythm (talam), improvisation (manodharmam) and expression (bhavam)."},{"Title":"Hindustani Classical Vocal","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 5-6 and Rules, Schedule II 5 & 6","Sections":{"About":["Solo. Separate competitions are held for male and female participants."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 10 minutes."],"Rules":["A Sruthi Box or a Thamburu is allowed.","One accompanist (Tabala) is allowed.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider pitch (sruthi), rhythm (layam), expression (bhavam) and rhythm cycle (talam).","Sound knowledge in the different Gharanas of Hindustani music, experience in Alaap rendering and improvisation in Swara patterns in Ragas are desirable. Sound knowledge in Tabala Talas in synchronising the music rendering and perfection in Sahithya Sudhi (clear words) are also desirable."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo. Separate competitions are held for male and female participants.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A Sruthi Box or a Thamburu is allowed.\\n- One accompanist (Tabala) is allowed.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider pitch (sruthi), rhythm (layam), expression (bhavam) and rhythm cycle (talam).\\n- Sound knowledge in the different Gharanas of Hindustani music, experience in Alaap rendering and improvisation in Swara patterns in Ragas are desirable. Sound knowledge in Tabala Talas in synchronising the music rendering and perfection in Sahithya Sudhi (clear words) are also desirable."},{"Title":"Gazal","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 7-8 and Rules, Schedule II 7 & 8","Sections":{"About":["Solo. Separate competitions are held for male and female participants. The item is open in any language."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 10 minutes."],"Rules":["Two accompanists are allowed (Harmonium and Tabala).","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider pitch (sruthi), rhythm (layam), expression (bhavam) and rhythm cycle (talam).","Creativity and improvisation in Gazal rendering with an impressive Raga pattern are preferred."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo. Separate competitions are held for male and female participants. The item is open in any language.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Two accompanists are allowed (Harmonium and Tabala).\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider pitch (sruthi), rhythm (layam), expression (bhavam) and rhythm cycle (talam).\\n- Creativity and improvisation in Gazal rendering with an impressive Raga pattern are preferred."},{"Title":"Mappilappattu","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 9-10 and Rules, Schedule II 9 & 10","Sections":{"About":["Solo. Separate competitions are held for male and female participants."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 5 minutes."],"Rules":["A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider the lyrics (sahityam), Mappila distinctiveness (Mappila thanima), rhythm (talam) and pitch and rhythm together (sruthilayam)."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo. Separate competitions are held for male and female participants.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider the lyrics (sahityam), Mappila distinctiveness (Mappila thanima), rhythm (talam) and pitch and rhythm together (sruthilayam)."},{"Title":"Veena","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 11 and Rules, Schedule II 11","Sections":{"About":["Solo, open to male and female."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 10 minutes."],"Rules":["A pick-up can be used.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider tone (nadam), raga expression (ragabhavam), rhythm (talam), the bowing (villittunnathu, as printed) and the plucking (meettu)."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo, open to male and female.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A pick-up can be used.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider tone (nadam), raga expression (ragabhavam), rhythm (talam), the bowing (villittunnathu, as printed) and the plucking (meettu)."},{"Title":"Stringed Instrument (Eastern Style)","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 12 and Rules, Schedule II 12","Sections":{"About":["Solo, open to male and female."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 10 minutes."],"Rules":["A pick-up can be used.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider pitch (sruthi), rhythm (layam) and expression (bhavam)."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo, open to male and female.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A pick-up can be used.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider pitch (sruthi), rhythm (layam) and expression (bhavam)."},{"Title":"Stringed Instrument (Western Style)","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 13 and Rules, Schedule II 13","Sections":{"About":["Solo, open to male and female."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 10 minutes."],"Rules":["A pick-up can be used.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider pitch (sruthi), rhythm (layam) and expression (bhavam)."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo, open to male and female.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A pick-up can be used.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider pitch (sruthi), rhythm (layam) and expression (bhavam)."},{"Title":"Guitar","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 14 and Rules, Schedule II 14 (Syndicate 30-1-2010, Item 76)","Sections":{"About":["Solo, open to male and female."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 10 minutes."],"Rules":["A pick-up can be used.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider pitch (sruthi), rhythm (layam) and expression (bhavam)."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo, open to male and female.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A pick-up can be used.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider pitch (sruthi), rhythm (layam) and expression (bhavam)."},{"Title":"Wind Instrument (Eastern Style)","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 15 and Rules, Schedule II 15","Sections":{"About":["Solo, open to male and female."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 10 minutes."],"Rules":["A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider rhythm (layam), expression (bhavam) and improvisation (manodharmam)."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo, open to male and female.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider rhythm (layam), expression (bhavam) and improvisation (manodharmam)."},{"Title":"Wind Instrument (Western Style)","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 16 and Rules, Schedule II 16","Sections":{"About":["Solo, open to male and female."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 10 minutes."],"Rules":["A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider rhythm (layam), expression (bhavam) and improvisation (manodharmam)."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo, open to male and female.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider rhythm (layam), expression (bhavam) and improvisation (manodharmam)."},{"Title":"Tabala","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 17 and Rules, Schedule II 17","Sections":{"About":["Solo, open to male and female."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 10 minutes."],"Rules":["A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider finger technique (anguli prayogam), tone (nadam) and rhythm (layam)."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo, open to male and female.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider finger technique (anguli prayogam), tone (nadam) and rhythm (layam)."},{"Title":"Percussion Instrument (Eastern Style)","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 18 and Rules, Schedule II 18","Sections":{"About":["Solo, open to male and female."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 10 minutes."],"Rules":["A pick-up can be used.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider tone (nadam), time measure (kalapramanam) and improvisation (manodharmam)."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo, open to male and female.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A pick-up can be used.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider tone (nadam), time measure (kalapramanam) and improvisation (manodharmam)."},{"Title":"Percussion Instrument (Western Style)","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 19 and Rules, Schedule II 19","Sections":{"About":["Solo, open to male and female."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 10 minutes."],"Rules":["A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider tone (nadam), time measure (kalapramanam) and improvisation (manodharmam)."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo, open to male and female.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider tone (nadam), time measure (kalapramanam) and improvisation (manodharmam)."},{"Title":"Chenda","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 20 and Rules, Schedule II 20","Sections":{"About":["Solo, open to male and female."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 10 minutes."],"Rules":["The competitor can use the chenda stick (chendakkol) in one hand only. The other hand plays without a stick.","The competitor can choose one of these koor (tala) as he or she likes: Chempakkoor, Adanthakkoor, Pancharikkoor.","Within the fixed time, the competitor must play the tala in four kalas: pathikalam, idavattam, idanila and iriyada.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo, open to male and female.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The competitor can use the chenda stick (chendakkol) in one hand only. The other hand plays without a stick.\\n- The competitor can choose one of these koor (tala) as he or she likes: Chempakkoor, Adanthakkoor, Pancharikkoor.\\n- Within the fixed time, the competitor must play the tala in four kalas: pathikalam, idavattam, idanila and iriyada.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given."},{"Title":"Western Vocal Solo","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 21 and Rules, Schedule II 21","Sections":{"About":["Solo, open to male and female."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 6 minutes. The song lasts between three and six minutes."],"Rules":["The number of accompanists must not be more than two.","The language of the song must be English only.","A pick-up can be used.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider composition, rhythm, co-ordination and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo, open to male and female.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 6 minutes. The song lasts between three and six minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The number of accompanists must not be more than two.\\n- The language of the song must be English only.\\n- A pick-up can be used.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider composition, rhythm, co-ordination and general impression."},{"Title":"Group Song","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 22 and Rules, Schedule II 22","Sections":{"About":["Team of 10 members."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 10 minutes."],"Rules":["A Sruthi Box can be used.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider pitch (sruthi), rhythm (talam), time (layam) and harmony of voices (swarachercha)."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Team of 10 members.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A Sruthi Box can be used.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider pitch (sruthi), rhythm (talam), time (layam) and harmony of voices (swarachercha)."},{"Title":"Western Vocal Group","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 23 and Rules, Schedule II 23","Sections":{"About":["Team of 6 members."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 10 minutes, which does not include setting time. The setting time for a group must not exceed four minutes."],"Rules":["The maximum number of singers in a group is six.","The maximum number of accompanists playing instruments is three.","The group song must be taken from the English language.","A Sruthi Box can be used.","A pick-up shall be used.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The item is judged on the quality of singing only, and not on make-up, costumes and action of the team."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Team of 6 members.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 10 minutes, which does not include setting time. The setting time for a group must not exceed four minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The maximum number of singers in a group is six.\\n- The maximum number of accompanists playing instruments is three.\\n- The group song must be taken from the English language.\\n- A Sruthi Box can be used.\\n- A pick-up shall be used.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The item is judged on the quality of singing only, and not on make-up, costumes and action of the team."},{"Title":"Ganamela","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 24 and Rules, Schedule II 24","Sections":{"About":["Team of at most 7 members."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is at most 10 minutes."],"Rules":["The instruments must be played by the competitors themselves.","Film songs are not allowed.","The songs should be written and set to music by students as far as possible.","All the music instruments must be played manually.","A Sruthi Box can be used.","A pick-up shall be used.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider pitch (sruthi), rhythm (talam) and the harmony between the different singers and the instruments."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Team of at most 7 members.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is at most 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The instruments must be played by the competitors themselves.\\n- Film songs are not allowed.\\n- The songs should be written and set to music by students as far as possible.\\n- All the music instruments must be played manually.\\n- A Sruthi Box can be used.\\n- A pick-up shall be used.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider pitch (sruthi), rhythm (talam) and the harmony between the different singers and the instruments."},{"Title":"Vrindavadyam","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 25 and Rules, Schedule II 25","Sections":{"About":["Team of at most 7 members."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is at most 10 minutes."],"Rules":["Western and Eastern style instruments can be used only by the competitors.","A Sruthi Box can be used.","A pick-up shall be used.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider tone (nadam), rhythm (talam), expression (bhavam), pitch (sruthi) and time (layam)."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Team of at most 7 members.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is at most 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Western and Eastern style instruments can be used only by the competitors.\\n- A Sruthi Box can be used.\\n- A pick-up shall be used.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider tone (nadam), rhythm (talam), expression (bhavam), pitch (sruthi) and time (layam)."},{"Title":"Folk Song","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 26 and Rules, Schedule II 26","Sections":{"About":["Team of at most 7 participants."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 10 minutes."],"Rules":["The tradition of the folk song must be shown on the stage.","The songs can be ritual songs (Anushtana Pattukal), farming songs (Krishi Pattukal) and Kali songs (Kali Pattukal).","Background music is prohibited. Karaoke is also prohibited.","No marks are given for the dress code.","At most 3 instruments can be used. The participants must play the instruments themselves.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Team of at most 7 participants.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The tradition of the folk song must be shown on the stage.\\n- The songs can be ritual songs (Anushtana Pattukal), farming songs (Krishi Pattukal) and Kali songs (Kali Pattukal).\\n- Background music is prohibited. Karaoke is also prohibited.\\n- No marks are given for the dress code.\\n- At most 3 instruments can be used. The participants must play the instruments themselves.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given."},{"Title":"Vanchipattu","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 27 and Rules, Schedule II 27","Sections":{"About":["Team of at most 10 members. It is an open competition for all."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is at most 10 minutes."],"Rules":["One of the 10 members is the rhythm keeper (thalakkaran). One is the lead singer (thalappattu). The other 8 are back singers.","The team can present the song in one style: the Vechupattu style, the Koottanadan style or the Aranmula style. The team must tell in advance, at the team registration, in which style it will present the Vanchipattu.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Rhythm (thalam) 20 marks. Pitch (sruthi) 20 marks. Unison of the singers 20 marks. Language purity 20 marks. Vaytthari (oral rhythm syllables) 20 marks."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Team of at most 10 members. It is an open competition for all.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is at most 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- One of the 10 members is the rhythm keeper (thalakkaran). One is the lead singer (thalappattu). The other 8 are back singers.\\n- The team can present the song in one style: the Vechupattu style, the Koottanadan style or the Aranmula style. The team must tell in advance, at the team registration, in which style it will present the Vanchipattu.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Rhythm (thalam) 20 marks. Pitch (sruthi) 20 marks. Unison of the singers 20 marks. Language purity 20 marks. Vaytthari (oral rhythm syllables) 20 marks."},{"Title":"Bharathanatyam","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 28-29 and Rules, Schedule II 28 & 29, 30 & 31 (one list for both items)","Sections":{"About":["Solo. Separate competitions are held for male and female participants."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 15 minutes."],"Rules":["Recorded music must be used.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider adavu (basic steps), rhythm (talam), mudra, expression (abhinayam), body discipline (meyvazhakkam), beauty of the costume (aharya shobha), footwork (chuvadveypp) and technical quality (sanketikatwam)."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo. Separate competitions are held for male and female participants.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 15 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Recorded music must be used.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider adavu (basic steps), rhythm (talam), mudra, expression (abhinayam), body discipline (meyvazhakkam), beauty of the costume (aharya shobha), footwork (chuvadveypp) and technical quality (sanketikatwam)."},{"Title":"Kuchipudi","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 30-31 and Rules, Schedule II 28 & 29, 30 & 31","Sections":{"About":["Solo. Separate competitions are held for male and female participants."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 15 minutes."],"Rules":["Recorded music must be used.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider adavu (basic steps), rhythm (talam), mudra, expression (abhinayam), body discipline (meyvazhakkam), beauty of the costume (aharya shobha), footwork (chuvadveypp) and technical quality (sanketikatwam)."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo. Separate competitions are held for male and female participants.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 15 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Recorded music must be used.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider adavu (basic steps), rhythm (talam), mudra, expression (abhinayam), body discipline (meyvazhakkam), beauty of the costume (aharya shobha), footwork (chuvadveypp) and technical quality (sanketikatwam)."},{"Title":"Folk Dance","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 32-33 and Rules, Schedule II 32 & 33","Sections":{"About":["Solo. Separate competitions are held for male and female participants."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 10 minutes."],"Rules":["Recorded music must be used.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider suitability of the costume, rhythm (talam), expression (bhavaprakatanam), body movement (angachalanam), footwork (chuvadveypp) and presentation (avatharanam)."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo. Separate competitions are held for male and female participants.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Recorded music must be used.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider suitability of the costume, rhythm (talam), expression (bhavaprakatanam), body movement (angachalanam), footwork (chuvadveypp) and presentation (avatharanam)."},{"Title":"Kathakali","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 34-35 and Rules, Schedule II 34 & 35","Sections":{"About":["Solo. Separate competitions are held for male and female participants."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 15 minutes."],"Rules":["A live orchestra is used in Kathakali.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider expression (bhavabhinayam), rhythm (talam), mudra, kalasam, body discipline (meyvazhakkam), improvisation (manodharmam), beauty of the costume (aharya shobha), technical quality (sanketikatwam) and the transformation into the role (veshapakarcha)."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo. Separate competitions are held for male and female participants.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 15 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A live orchestra is used in Kathakali.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider expression (bhavabhinayam), rhythm (talam), mudra, kalasam, body discipline (meyvazhakkam), improvisation (manodharmam), beauty of the costume (aharya shobha), technical quality (sanketikatwam) and the transformation into the role (veshapakarcha)."},{"Title":"Mohiniyattam","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 36 and Rules, Schedule II 36","Sections":{"About":["Solo, for female participants."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 15 minutes."],"Rules":["Recorded music must be used.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider adavu (basic steps), rhythm (talam), mudra, expression (abhinayam), body discipline (meyvazhakkam), beauty of the costume (aharya shobha), footwork (chuvadveypp) and technical quality (sanketikatwam)."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo, for female participants.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 15 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Recorded music must be used.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider adavu (basic steps), rhythm (talam), mudra, expression (abhinayam), body discipline (meyvazhakkam), beauty of the costume (aharya shobha), footwork (chuvadveypp) and technical quality (sanketikatwam)."},{"Title":"Ottam Thullal","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 37-38 and Rules, Schedule II 37 & 38 (Syndicate 15-12-89, Item 8)","Sections":{"About":["Solo. Separate competitions are held for male and female participants."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 10 minutes."],"Rules":["A live orchestra is used in Ottamthullal.","The back singers must not sing in place of the performer without letting the performer sing. The performers must sing first, so that the judges can understand their knowledge of music.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider costume style (veshabhangi), fineness of the costume (veshathinte sookshmata), clarity of the letters (aksharasphutata), musical quality (sangeethagunam), expression (abhinayam) and rhythm (talam)."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo. Separate competitions are held for male and female participants.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A live orchestra is used in Ottamthullal.\\n- The back singers must not sing in place of the performer without letting the performer sing. The performers must sing first, so that the judges can understand their knowledge of music.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider costume style (veshabhangi), fineness of the costume (veshathinte sookshmata), clarity of the letters (aksharasphutata), musical quality (sangeethagunam), expression (abhinayam) and rhythm (talam)."},{"Title":"Group Dance","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 39 and Rules, Schedule II 39","Sections":{"About":["Team of 10 members."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 10 minutes."],"Rules":["A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider the coordination among the dancers, costume design, suitability of the costume, movement together, rhythm (talam), presentation and the idea."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Team of 10 members.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider the coordination among the dancers, costume design, suitability of the costume, movement together, rhythm (talam), presentation and the idea."},{"Title":"Thiruvathira","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 40 and Rules, Schedule II 40 (Syndicate 5-12-89, Item 8); Amendments, Dance section 2","Sections":{"About":["Team of 10 members. Girls only."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 10 minutes."],"Rules":["Up to ten persons can take part. Only three persons are allowed to sing in the background.","A sruthi is allowed in the background. Tabala, mridangam, edakka, violin and other musical instruments are not allowed.","Certificates are issued to at most 8 performers and 2 accompanists.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Team of 10 members. Girls only.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Up to ten persons can take part. Only three persons are allowed to sing in the background.\\n- A sruthi is allowed in the background. Tabala, mridangam, edakka, violin and other musical instruments are not allowed.\\n- Certificates are issued to at most 8 performers and 2 accompanists.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given."},{"Title":"Oppana","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 41 and Rules, Schedule II 41","Sections":{"About":["Team of 10 members. Girls only."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 10 minutes."],"Rules":["There is no side music (pakkamelam) and no background singing.","Lead singers (munpattukar) are a must, and back singers are needed. The others join in the singing.","The song and the clapping that matches the rhythm are the main parts.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider the tune (isal) of the Oppana song, the combination of rhythm and clapping, the literary quality of the song, pitch and rhythm and word style (sruthilayam, shabdabhangi) and the distinctive presentation."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Team of 10 members. Girls only.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- There is no side music (pakkamelam) and no background singing.\\n- Lead singers (munpattukar) are a must, and back singers are needed. The others join in the singing.\\n- The song and the clapping that matches the rhythm are the main parts.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider the tune (isal) of the Oppana song, the combination of rhythm and clapping, the literary quality of the song, pitch and rhythm and word style (sruthilayam, shabdabhangi) and the distinctive presentation."},{"Title":"Margamkali","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 42 and Rules, Schedule II 42; Amendments, Dance section 3","Sections":{"About":["Team of 7 members. Girls only."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 10 minutes."],"Rules":["A traditional lamp (nilavilakku) as the stage property is a must.","A small cymbal (kuzhithalam) can be used to keep the rhythm. Other musical instruments and background singing are not allowed.","Certificates are issued to at most 6 performers and 1 accompanist.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider the costume (vesham), the song (pattu), the steps (chuvadu) and the movement (chalanam)."],"Points":null,"Notes":["Schedule I and the Margamkali judging text print 7 members; the amendment on certificates names 6 performers and 1 accompanist."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Team of 7 members. Girls only.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A traditional lamp (nilavilakku) as the stage property is a must.\\n- A small cymbal (kuzhithalam) can be used to keep the rhythm. Other musical instruments and background singing are not allowed.\\n- Certificates are issued to at most 6 performers and 1 accompanist.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider the costume (vesham), the song (pattu), the steps (chuvadu) and the movement (chalanam).\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- Schedule I and the Margamkali judging text print 7 members; the amendment on certificates names 6 performers and 1 accompanist."},{"Title":"Kerala Nadanam","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 43-44 and Rules, Schedule II 43-45","Sections":{"About":["Solo. Separate competitions are held for male and female participants."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 15 minutes."],"Rules":["A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider the costume (veshavidhanam), clarity of the mudra, footwork in step with the rhythm (talanusarana chuvadveypp), expression (bhavabhinayam) and the distinctiveness (thanima) of Kerala Nadanam."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo. Separate competitions are held for male and female participants.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 15 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider the costume (veshavidhanam), clarity of the mudra, footwork in step with the rhythm (talanusarana chuvadveypp), expression (bhavabhinayam) and the distinctiveness (thanima) of Kerala Nadanam."},{"Title":"Kerala Nadanam Group","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 45 and Rules, Schedule II 45","Sections":{"About":["Team of 10 members."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 30 minutes."],"Rules":["A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider the costume (veshavidhanam), clarity of the mudra, footwork in step with the rhythm (talanusarana chuvadveypp), expression (bhavabhinayam) and the distinctiveness (thanima) of Kerala Nadanam."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Team of 10 members.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider the costume (veshavidhanam), clarity of the mudra, footwork in step with the rhythm (talanusarana chuvadveypp), expression (bhavabhinayam) and the distinctiveness (thanima) of Kerala Nadanam."},{"Title":"Dufmutt","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 46 and Rules, Schedule II 46 (Syndicate 23-11-2015, Items 12.19 and 12.20)","Sections":{"About":["Team of 10 members. Boys only."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 10 minutes."],"Rules":["The item must have any four talas of these: Ottamuttu, Moonnumuttu, Anjmuttu, Kayinmuttu, Korimuttu.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider the baith (song), the talas, the playing of the instrument (vadyavadanam) and the presentation."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Team of 10 members. Boys only.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The item must have any four talas of these: Ottamuttu, Moonnumuttu, Anjmuttu, Kayinmuttu, Korimuttu.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider the baith (song), the talas, the playing of the instrument (vadyavadanam) and the presentation."},{"Title":"Kolkali","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 47 and Rules, Schedule II 47","Sections":{"About":["Team of 12 members. Boys only."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 10 minutes."],"Rules":["A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider the distinctiveness of the song, the combination of rhythm and the kol (stick), body movement (meythayam), footwork (chuvaduveypp) and the distinctive presentation."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Team of 12 members. Boys only.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider the distinctiveness of the song, the combination of rhythm and the kol (stick), body movement (meythayam), footwork (chuvaduveypp) and the distinctive presentation."},{"Title":"Chakyarkoothu","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 48 and Rules, Schedule II 48","Sections":{"About":["Solo."],"TimeAndFormat":["The longest time is 20 minutes. The singing (ganalapanam) takes 5 minutes."],"Rules":["Songs composed in Sanskrit are sung.","Priority is given to light music (lalitha sangeetham).","One mizhavu player is the accompanist. The accompanist need not be a student.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Costume style (veshabhangi) 20 marks. Result (phalitham) 20 marks. Clarity of the letters (aksharasphutata) 20 marks. Literary style (sahithyabhangi) 20 marks. Presentation skill (avatarana patutwam) 20 marks."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The longest time is 20 minutes. The singing (ganalapanam) takes 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Songs composed in Sanskrit are sung.\\n- Priority is given to light music (lalitha sangeetham).\\n- One mizhavu player is the accompanist. The accompanist need not be a student.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Costume style (veshabhangi) 20 marks. Result (phalitham) 20 marks. Clarity of the letters (aksharasphutata) 20 marks. Literary style (sahithyabhangi) 20 marks. Presentation skill (avatarana patutwam) 20 marks."},{"Title":"Nangyarkoothu","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 49 and Rules, Schedule II 49","Sections":{"About":["Solo."],"TimeAndFormat":["The longest time is 20 minutes."],"Rules":["The accompaniment (pakkamelam) is 2 mizhavu players, 1 edakka player and 1 thalam player (4 persons in all). They need not be students.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["Costume style (veshabhangi) 20 marks. Body culture (shareerasamskaram) 20 marks. Mudra 20 marks. Rasa expression (rasapushti) 20 marks. Stage presentation (rangavatarana) 10 marks. Sense of rhythm (talabodham) 10 marks."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The longest time is 20 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The accompaniment (pakkamelam) is 2 mizhavu players, 1 edakka player and 1 thalam player (4 persons in all). They need not be students.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Costume style (veshabhangi) 20 marks. Body culture (shareerasamskaram) 20 marks. Mudra 20 marks. Rasa expression (rasapushti) 20 marks. Stage presentation (rangavatarana) 10 marks. Sense of rhythm (talabodham) 10 marks."},{"Title":"Vattapattu","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 101 and Rules, Schedule II 101 (U.O. dated 17-02-2020)","Sections":{"About":["Team of 10 members. Boys only."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 10 minutes."],"Rules":["There is no side music (pakkamelam) and no background singing.","Lead singers (munpattukar) are a must, and back singers are needed. The others join in the singing.","The song and the clapping that matches the rhythm are the main parts.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider the tune (isal) of the Vattapattu, the combination of rhythm and clapping, the literary quality of the song, pitch and rhythm and word style, and the distinctive presentation."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Team of 10 members. Boys only.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- There is no side music (pakkamelam) and no background singing.\\n- Lead singers (munpattukar) are a must, and back singers are needed. The others join in the singing.\\n- The song and the clapping that matches the rhythm are the main parts.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider the tune (isal) of the Vattapattu, the combination of rhythm and clapping, the literary quality of the song, pitch and rhythm and word style, and the distinctive presentation."},{"Title":"Arabanamuttu","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 102 and Rules, Schedule II 102 (U.O. dated 17-02-2020)","Sections":{"About":["Team of 10 members. Boys only."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 10 minutes."],"Rules":["A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider the baith, pitch and rhythm (sruthitalam), expression (bhavam), body movement and the playing of the instrument (meythayam, vadyavadanam) and the presentation."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Team of 10 members. Boys only.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider the baith, pitch and rhythm (sruthitalam), expression (bhavam), body movement and the playing of the instrument (meythayam, vadyavadanam) and the presentation."},{"Title":"Debate","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 50-52 and Rules, Schedule II 50-52","Sections":{"About":["Team of 2 members. The item is held in English, Malayalam and Hindi."],"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["The rules print no time and no judging aspects for Debate."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Team of 2 members. The item is held in English, Malayalam and Hindi.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- The rules print no time and no judging aspects for Debate."},{"Title":"Elocution","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 53-58 and Rules, Schedule II 53-58","Sections":{"About":["Solo. The item is held in Malayalam, English, Hindi, Sanskrit, Arabic and Tamil."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 5 minutes."],"Rules":["A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["The rules print no judging aspects for Elocution."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo. The item is held in Malayalam, English, Hindi, Sanskrit, Arabic and Tamil.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- The rules print no judging aspects for Elocution."},{"Title":"Recitation","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 59-64 and Rules, Schedule II 59-64","Sections":{"About":["Solo. The item is held in Malayalam, English, Hindi, Sanskrit, Arabic and Tamil."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 5 minutes."],"Rules":["A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider memorising (manahpaatham), clarity of the letters (aksharasphutata), restrained expression (mitamaya bhavaprakatanam) and the understanding of the meaning and idea."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo. The item is held in Malayalam, English, Hindi, Sanskrit, Arabic and Tamil.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider memorising (manahpaatham), clarity of the letters (aksharasphutata), restrained expression (mitamaya bhavaprakatanam) and the understanding of the meaning and idea."},{"Title":"Essay Writing","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 65-68 and Rules, Schedule II 65-68","Sections":{"About":["Solo. The item is held in Malayalam, English, Hindi and Tamil."],"TimeAndFormat":["The time is 1 hour."],"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["The rules print no judging aspects for Essay Writing."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo. The item is held in Malayalam, English, Hindi and Tamil.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The time is 1 hour.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- The rules print no judging aspects for Essay Writing."},{"Title":"Short Story Writing","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 69-74 and Rules, Schedule II 69-74","Sections":{"About":["Solo. The item is held in Malayalam, English, Hindi, Sanskrit, Arabic and Tamil."],"TimeAndFormat":["The time is 1 hour."],"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["The rules print no judging aspects for Short Story Writing."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo. The item is held in Malayalam, English, Hindi, Sanskrit, Arabic and Tamil.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The time is 1 hour.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- The rules print no judging aspects for Short Story Writing."},{"Title":"Poetry Writing","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 75-80 and Rules, Schedule II 75-80","Sections":{"About":["Solo. The item is held in Malayalam, English, Hindi, Sanskrit, Arabic and Tamil."],"TimeAndFormat":["The time is 1 hour."],"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["The rules print no judging aspects for Poetry Writing."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo. The item is held in Malayalam, English, Hindi, Sanskrit, Arabic and Tamil.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The time is 1 hour.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- The rules print no judging aspects for Poetry Writing."},{"Title":"Aksharaslokam","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 81-83 and Rules, Schedule II 81-83","Sections":{"About":["Solo. The item is held in Malayalam, Sanskrit and Arabic."],"TimeAndFormat":["The time is fixed by the judges."],"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider clarity of the letters (aksharasphutata), understanding of the meaning (arthavabodham), richness of ideas (ashayapaushkalyam) and the ability to answer quickly."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo. The item is held in Malayalam, Sanskrit and Arabic.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The time is fixed by the judges.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider clarity of the letters (aksharasphutata), understanding of the meaning (arthavabodham), richness of ideas (ashayapaushkalyam) and the ability to answer quickly."},{"Title":"Quiz","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 84 and Rules, Schedule II 84","Sections":{"About":["Team of 2 members."],"TimeAndFormat":["The time is fixed by the judges."],"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["The rules print no other rule and no judging aspects for Quiz."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Team of 2 members.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The time is fixed by the judges.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- The rules print no other rule and no judging aspects for Quiz."},{"Title":"Kathaprasangam","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 85-86 and Rules, Schedule II 85-86; Amendments, Theatre Events 1","Sections":{"About":["Solo. Separate competitions are held for male and female participants. It is a Theatre Event."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 20 minutes."],"Rules":["Three accompanists (students or professionals) are allowed.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider clarity of the letters (aksharashuddhi), purity of language (bhashashuddhi), purity of the idea (ashayashuddhi), expression (bhavaprakatanam) and the proportion of literature and song."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo. Separate competitions are held for male and female participants. It is a Theatre Event.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 20 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Three accompanists (students or professionals) are allowed.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider clarity of the letters (aksharashuddhi), purity of language (bhashashuddhi), purity of the idea (ashayashuddhi), expression (bhavaprakatanam) and the proportion of literature and song."},{"Title":"Mono Act","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 87-88 and Rules, Schedule II 87-88","Sections":{"About":["Solo. Separate competitions are held for male and female participants."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 5 minutes."],"Rules":["A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider the story (kathavastu), memorising (manahpaatham), acting (abhinayam), naturalness (thanmayatwam), purity of the text (sahityashuddhi) and originality of the idea (maulikashayam)."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo. Separate competitions are held for male and female participants.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider the story (kathavastu), memorising (manahpaatham), acting (abhinayam), naturalness (thanmayatwam), purity of the text (sahityashuddhi) and originality of the idea (maulikashayam)."},{"Title":"Mimicry","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 89-90 and Rules, Schedule II 89-90","Sections":{"About":["Solo. Separate competitions are held for male and female participants."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 5 minutes."],"Rules":["A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider originality of the idea (maulikashayam), voice control (shabdasvadhinata), improvisation (manodharmam) and skill in imitation (anukarana patavam)."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo. Separate competitions are held for male and female participants.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider originality of the idea (maulikashayam), voice control (shabdasvadhinata), improvisation (manodharmam) and skill in imitation (anukarana patavam)."},{"Title":"Fancy Dress","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 91 and Rules, Schedule II 91 (Syndicate 5-12-89, Item 8)","Sections":{"About":["Solo."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 3 minutes."],"Rules":["The costume is the main thing.","Movement is needed.","Speech is not allowed.","Background sound can be arranged. Robot, post box, missile and the like must be avoided.","No one else sings along with the performer.","The costume must not be of a type that hides the person completely.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 3 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The costume is the main thing.\\n- Movement is needed.\\n- Speech is not allowed.\\n- Background sound can be arranged. Robot, post box, missile and the like must be avoided.\\n- No one else sings along with the performer.\\n- The costume must not be of a type that hides the person completely.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given."},{"Title":"Mime","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 92 and Rules, Schedule II 92 (Syndicate 5-12-89, Item 8)","Sections":{"About":["Team of at most 6 members."],"TimeAndFormat":["Performing time is 5 minutes."],"Rules":["A mask can be used.","Mime is silent acting. Facial expression is its main part and speech is not allowed.","A microphone is not used on the stage.","Background sound can be arranged.","Movement is the speciality of this item.","A live orchestra, recorded music or both together can be used.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Team of at most 6 members.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- Performing time is 5 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- A mask can be used.\\n- Mime is silent acting. Facial expression is its main part and speech is not allowed.\\n- A microphone is not used on the stage.\\n- Background sound can be arranged.\\n- Movement is the speciality of this item.\\n- A live orchestra, recorded music or both together can be used.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given."},{"Title":"Skit","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 93 and Rules, Schedule II 93 (Syndicate 5-12-89, Item 8); Amendments, Theatre Events 2","Sections":{"About":["Team of at least 2 and at most 6 members."],"TimeAndFormat":["The longest time is 10 minutes."],"Rules":["Make-up, drapery and background music can be used.","No personal remark or character assassination is allowed.","A live orchestra, recorded music or both together can be used.","A grace time of 30 seconds is given."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The item is judged on theme, work on acting, stage craft, total design and general impression."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Team of at least 2 and at most 6 members.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The longest time is 10 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Make-up, drapery and background music can be used.\\n- No personal remark or character assassination is allowed.\\n- A live orchestra, recorded music or both together can be used.\\n- A grace time of 30 seconds is given.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The item is judged on theme, work on acting, stage craft, total design and general impression."},{"Title":"Painting","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 94 and Rules, Schedule II 94","Sections":{"About":["Solo."],"TimeAndFormat":["The time is 2 hours."],"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider the relation with the subject, the combination of colours, the arrangement of lines (rekhavinyasam), the personal style and the composition."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The time is 2 hours.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider the relation with the subject, the combination of colours, the arrangement of lines (rekhavinyasam), the personal style and the composition."},{"Title":"Clay Modelling","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 95 and Rules, Schedule II 95","Sections":{"About":["Solo. The Committee recommended the word Clay Modelling instead of Sculpture."],"TimeAndFormat":["The time is 3 hours."],"Rules":["Only the clay provided by the organisers can be used."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":["The judges consider the subject, the three dimensional form, the composition, completeness, the personal style and the finish (mizhivu)."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo. The Committee recommended the word Clay Modelling instead of Sculpture.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The time is 3 hours.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- Only the clay provided by the organisers can be used.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- The judges consider the subject, the three dimensional form, the composition, completeness, the personal style and the finish (mizhivu)."},{"Title":"Cartooning","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 96 and Rules, Schedule II 96","Sections":{"About":["Solo."],"TimeAndFormat":["The time is 2 hours."],"Rules":null,"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":["The rules print no other rule and no judging aspects for Cartooning."]},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The time is 2 hours.\\n\\n## Notes for participants\\n- The rules print no other rule and no judging aspects for Cartooning."},{"Title":"Rangoli","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 97 and Rules, Schedule II 97","Sections":{"About":["Solo."],"TimeAndFormat":["The time is not more than two and a half hours (2.30 hours)."],"Rules":["The participants bring their own materials for this event.","The medium and the form of expression can be free hand, pictorial and descriptive."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The time is not more than two and a half hours (2.30 hours).\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The participants bring their own materials for this event.\\n- The medium and the form of expression can be free hand, pictorial and descriptive."},{"Title":"Collage","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 98 and Rules, Schedule II 98","Sections":{"About":["Solo. The item is held on the spot."],"TimeAndFormat":["The time is not more than 2.30 hours."],"Rules":["The participants bring their own scissors and pasting materials."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo. The item is held on the spot.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The time is not more than 2.30 hours.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The participants bring their own scissors and pasting materials."},{"Title":"Spot Photography","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 99 and Rules, Schedule II 99","Sections":{"About":["Solo."],"TimeAndFormat":["The time limit is 2.30 hours."],"Rules":["The digital camera must have a memory card, which the judges format before the contest starts.","The participant must take 5 photographs on the theme that the judges announce on the spot.","The participant brings his or her own digital camera.","The organisers have all rights to use these pictures as and when they think fit.","Additional instructions are announced on the spot."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":["No mixing, matching or morphing of photographs is permitted.","Software such as Photoshop to improve images is not permitted."],"Judging":["Digital images are judged on impact, composition, technical quality and suitability for the specific theme."],"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The time limit is 2.30 hours.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The digital camera must have a memory card, which the judges format before the contest starts.\\n- The participant must take 5 photographs on the theme that the judges announce on the spot.\\n- The participant brings his or her own digital camera.\\n- The organisers have all rights to use these pictures as and when they think fit.\\n- Additional instructions are announced on the spot.\\n\\n## Not allowed\\n- No mixing, matching or morphing of photographs is permitted.\\n- Software such as Photoshop to improve images is not permitted.\\n\\n## Judging\\n- Digital images are judged on impact, composition, technical quality and suitability for the specific theme."},{"Title":"Poster Making","Source":"Rules, Schedule I 100 and Rules, Schedule II 100","Sections":{"About":["Solo. The item is held on the spot."],"TimeAndFormat":["The time is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes."],"Rules":["The participants make a poster on the subject, topic or theme given by the in-charge of the competition.","The participants bring their own materials. Only the drawing paper or sheet of 22 inch x 15 inch is provided by the organisers."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## About this competition\\n- Solo. The item is held on the spot.\\n\\n## Time and format\\n- The time is not more than 2 hours 30 minutes.\\n\\n## Rules\\n- The participants make a poster on the subject, topic or theme given by the in-charge of the competition.\\n- The participants bring their own materials. Only the drawing paper or sheet of 22 inch x 15 inch is provided by the organisers."}]'),s=[],l=[{Key:"CollegeLevelTiming",Kind:"text",Label:"When the college level competitions are held",Value:"Not later than the second week of November every year",Source:"Rules 6, p.2"},{Key:"EntryFormDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Last date for the entry form to reach the General Secretary of the Kerala University Union",Value:"10 November",Source:"Rules 11, p.3"},{Key:"UniversityFestivalTiming",Kind:"text",Label:"When the University level Youth Festival is held, by the rules",Value:"Before the Christmas holidays every year",Source:"Rules 12(a), p.3"},{Key:"EventStartDate",Kind:"date",Label:"First day of the 2025 University Youth Festival",Value:"2025-05-28",Source:"Brochure 2025, cover and p.3"},{Key:"EventEndDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Last day of the 2025 University Youth Festival",Value:"2025-05-31",Source:"Brochure 2025, cover and p.7"},{Key:"Venue",Kind:"address",Label:"Venue of the University Youth Festival (2025 edition)",Value:{Name:"Eleven venues in Kollam city",Address:"Sree Narayana College Kollam (ONV Nagar and the Chemistry Lab); Sree Narayana College for Women (open air auditorium and auditorium); TKM College of Arts and Science, Kollam (and its seminar hall); C. Kesavan Memorial Town Hall; Fatima Memorial Training College, Pallimukku; University Institute of Technology, Mulamkhadakam; Fatima Mata National College, Cathalani campus (self financing)",City:"Kollam",MapUrl:"",Directions:""},Source:"Brochure 2025, pp.2-8"},{Key:"ReceptionCommittee",Kind:"contact",Label:"Reception Committee, Youth Festival 2025",Value:{Name:"Sri. M. Noushad (MLA), Chairman; R. Gopikrishnan, Convenor",Role:"Reception Committee",Phone:"",WhatsApp:"",Email:""},Source:"Brochure 2025, p.2"},{Key:"ProgrammeCommittee",Kind:"contact",Label:"Programme Committee, Youth Festival 2025",Value:{Name:"Dr. Nithya U S, Chairman; Karthik Anand S, Convenor",Role:"Programme Committee",Phone:"",WhatsApp:"",Email:""},Source:"Brochure 2025, p.2"},{Key:"KeralaUniversityUnion",Kind:"contact",Label:"Kerala University Union, Youth Festival 2025",Value:{Name:"Aswin S, Chairman; Govind A V, General Secretary",Role:"Kerala University Union (receives the entry forms)",Phone:"",WhatsApp:"",Email:""},Source:"Brochure 2025, p.2"},{Key:"RulesOrder",Kind:"text",Label:"Order that issued the Rules",Value:"No. DSS/19/KUYF/2024 dated 20-02-2024, Department of Student Services, University of Kerala, Thiruvananthapuram",Source:"Rules, Abstract, p.1"},{Key:"Announcements",Kind:"news",Label:"News printed in the 2025 brochure",Value:[{Date:"2025-05-28",Title:"Kerala University Union Youth Festival 2025, Kollam, 28 to 31 May",Text:"The Kerala University Union announced the largest youth festival of Asia in Kollam city on 28, 29, 30 and 31 May 2025. About 5000 talented youth from more than 250 colleges affiliated to the University of Kerala take part in 116 cultural events at eleven venues.",Url:"https://kuyf.keralauniversity.ac.in/images/Youth_festival_2025_official_schedule.pdf"},{Date:"2025-05-28",Title:"Day 1, Wednesday 28 May",Text:"ONV Nagar (SN College Kollam): 10:00 am Thiruvathira, 3:00 pm Inaugural Function, 5:00 pm Mohiniyattam. G Devarajan Master Nagar (SN College for Women, open air auditorium): 10:00 am Chakyarkoothu, 12:00 pm Nangyarkoothu, 1:00 pm Ottamthullal (Transgender), 2:00 pm Ottamthullal (Female), 5:00 pm Ottamthullal (Male). Bharat Murali Nagar (TKM Arts College): 10:00 am Oppana, 2:00 pm Elocution (Arabic), 3:00 pm Recitation (Arabic), 5:00 pm Aksharaslokam (Arabic). O Madhavan Nagar (C. Kesavan Memorial Town Hall): 10:00 am Classical Music (Transgender), 11:00 am Classical Music (Female), 4:00 pm Classical Music (Male). P S Banarji Nagar (SN College for Women, auditorium): 10:00 am Folk Song. K P Appan Nagar (Fatima Memorial Training College, Pallimukk): 10:00 am Hindustani Classical (Female), 12:00 pm Hindustani Classical (Male), 2:00 pm Hindustani Classical (Transgender), 3:00 pm Gazal (Female), 6:00 pm Gazal (Transgender), 7:00 pm Gazal (Male). V Sambasivan Nagar (UIT Mulamkhadakam): 10:00 am Kathakali (Female), 12:00 pm Kathakali (Male), 2:00 pm Kathakali (Transgender), 3:00 pm Recitation (Tamil), 5:00 pm Elocution (Tamil). Jayan Nagar (Fatima Mata National College, Cathalani campus): 3:00 pm Margamkali. Chavara Parukuttyamma Nagar (SN College Kollam Chemistry Lab): 9:00 am Cartooning, 11:00 am Rangoli, 2:00 pm Clay Modelling. Kottarakkara Sreedharan Nair Nagar (TKM Arts College seminar hall): 10:00 am Group Song. Kakkanadan Nagar (Fatima Mata National College, Cathalani campus): 9:00 am Essay Writing (Tamil), 10:00 am Essay Writing (English), 11:00 am Essay Writing (Hindi), 12:00 pm Essay Writing (Malayalam), 1:00 pm Short Story Writing (Malayalam), 2:00 pm (English), 3:00 pm (Sanskrit), 4:00 pm (Tamil), 5:00 pm (Arabic), 6:00 pm (Hindi).",Url:"https://kuyf.keralauniversity.ac.in/images/Youth_festival_2025_official_schedule.pdf"},{Date:"2025-05-29",Title:"Day 2, Thursday 29 May",Text:"ONV Nagar: 9:00 am Kerala Nadanam (Female), 12:00 pm Kerala Nadanam (Transgender), 1:00 pm Kerala Nadanam (Male), 5:00 pm Kerala Nadanam Group. G Devarajan Master Nagar: 9:00 am Light Music (Transgender), 9:30 am Light Music (Female), 5:00 pm Light Music (Male). Bharat Murali Nagar: 9:00 am Kolkali, 12:00 pm Duffmutt, 2:00 pm Arabanamutt, 4:00 pm Vattapattu. O Madhavan Nagar: 9:00 am Bharatanatyam (Transgender), 10:00 am Bharatanatyam (Male), 12:00 pm Bharatanatyam (Female), 5:00 pm Skit. P S Banarji Nagar: 9:00 am Recitation (Hindi), 11:00 am Elocution (Hindi), 12:00 pm Debate (Hindi), 3:00 pm Mime. K P Appan Nagar: 9:00 am Recitation (Sanskrit), 12:00 pm Elocution (Sanskrit), 1:00 pm Aksharaslokam (Sanskrit), 4:00 pm Veena, 5:00 pm Guitar. V Sambasivan Nagar: 9:00 am Aksharaslokam (Malayalam). Jayan Nagar: 9:00 am Elocution (English), 12:00 pm Debate (English), 2:00 pm Western Vocal Solo, 4:00 pm Western Vocal Group. Chavara Parukuttyamma Nagar: 9:00 am Poetry Writing (Arabic), 10:00 am (Tamil), 11:00 am (Sanskrit), 12:00 pm (Hindi), 2:00 pm (English), 3:00 pm (Malayalam). Kottarakkara Sreedharan Nair Nagar: 9:00 am String Instrument Eastern, 11:00 am String Instrument Western, 1:00 pm Wind Instrument Eastern, 2:00 pm Wind Instrument Western, 3:00 pm Percussion Instrument Eastern, 5:00 pm Percussion Instrument Western. Kakkanadan Nagar: 9:00 am Painting, 11:00 am Spot Photography, 1:00 pm Collage, 3:30 pm Poster Making.",Url:"https://kuyf.keralauniversity.ac.in/images/Youth_festival_2025_official_schedule.pdf"},{Date:"2025-05-30",Title:"Day 3, Friday 30 May",Text:"ONV Nagar: 9:00 am Fancy Dress, 12:00 pm Folk Dance (Transgender), 1:00 pm Folk Dance (Male), 3:00 pm Folk Dance (Female), 5:00 pm Group Dance. G Devarajan Master Nagar: 9:00 am Kuchippudi (Transgender), 10:00 am Kuchippudi (Male), 12:00 pm Kuchippudi (Female). Bharat Murali Nagar: 9:00 am Vanchipattu, 6:00 pm Drama. P S Banarji Nagar: 9:00 am Mono Act (Transgender), 10:00 am Mono Act (Female), 12:00 pm Mono Act (Male), 3:00 pm Ganamela, 6:00 pm Vrindavadhyam. K P Appan Nagar: 9:00 am Mappilapattu (Transgender), 10:00 am Mappilapattu (Female), 2:00 pm Mappilapattu (Male). V Sambasivan Nagar: 9:00 am Tabala, 11:00 am Chenda, 3:00 pm Kathaprasangam (Transgender), 5:00 pm Kathaprasangam (Female), 6:00 pm Kathaprasangam (Male). Chavara Parukuttyamma Nagar: 9:00 am Recitation (Malayalam). Kottarakkara Sreedharan Nair Nagar: 9:00 am Recitation (English), 4:00 pm Quiz. Kakkanadan Nagar: 10:00 am Debate (Malayalam), 2:00 pm Elocution (Malayalam).",Url:"https://kuyf.keralauniversity.ac.in/images/Youth_festival_2025_official_schedule.pdf"},{Date:"2025-05-31",Title:"Day 4, Saturday 31 May",Text:"ONV Nagar (SN College Kollam): 9:00 am Mimicry (Transgender), 10:00 am Mimicry (Female), 11:00 am Mimicry (Male), 4:00 pm Valedictory Function, 5:00 pm Prize Distribution, 6:00 pm Variety Entertainments by Festival Winners.",Url:"https://kuyf.keralauniversity.ac.in/images/Youth_festival_2025_official_schedule.pdf"}],Source:"Brochure 2025, pp.1-8"},{Key:"EventWebsite",Kind:"link",Label:"Festival website of the University of Kerala (results, rules, programme)",Value:"https://kuyf.keralauniversity.ac.in/",Source:"Website home page"}],r=[{Claim:"Rules 1-34, the Syndicate amendments and the appendix (college and University level, eligibility, appeals, judges, points, championships), Schedule I (items, team sizes, performing times) and Schedule II (judging aspects and item rules) are taken from the University's rules.",SourceType:"Primary - University of Kerala official 'Kerala University Youth Festival Rules 2024' (Department of Student Services, No. DSS/19/KUYF/2024)",Source:"Kerala University Youth Festival Rules 2024, pp.1-20",Url:"https://kuyf.keralauniversity.ac.in/images/Youth-Festival-Rules-2024.pdf"},{Claim:"The 2025 rules file on the festival website has the same text as the 2024 file (the 2024 cover page is not in it).",SourceType:"Primary - the University's festival website",Source:"Youth Festival Rules 2025 (PDF), kuyf.keralauniversity.ac.in",Url:"https://kuyf.keralauniversity.ac.in/images/Youth-Festival-Rules-2025.pdf"},{Claim:"The 2025 edition: dates (28 to 31 May 2025), the Kollam venues, the organising committees and the programme by day.",SourceType:"Primary - the University's festival website",Source:"Youth Festival 2025 brochure and official schedule (PDF)",Url:"https://kuyf.keralauniversity.ac.in/images/Youth_festival_2025_official_schedule.pdf"}],h={TemplateKey:e,Year:2025,Note:a,Page:t,ParticipantTypes:n,AgeGroups:i,Competitions:o,CompetitionAgeGroups:s,Variables:l,Evidence:r};export{i as AgeGroups,s as CompetitionAgeGroups,o as Competitions,r as Evidence,a as Note,t as Page,n as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,l as Variables,m as Year,h as default};
